' ============================================================================
' TECHNICAL NOTES
' ============================================================================

note right of UserEntity
  **Authentication & Authorization**
  - BCrypt password hashing
  - JWT token-based auth
  - Email verification required
  - Soft delete via deletedAt
  - Page visit tracking
end note

note right of RoleEntity
  **Role-Based Access Control**
  USER: Default role, forum access
  ADMIN: Full system access
  
  Eagerly loaded for performance
end note

note bottom of Post
  **Forum Post Management**
  - Author is mandatory
  - Tags via join table (post_tags)
  - Comments cascade deleted
  - Timestamp auto-generated
end note

note bottom of Comment
  **Validation & Lifecycle**
  - Max 10,000 characters
  - Timestamp via @PrePersist
  - Timezone: Europe/Amsterdam
  - Immutable after creation
end note

note left of PasswordResetToken
  **Security Flow**
  1. User requests reset
  2. Token generated (unique)
  3. Email sent with link
  4. Token expires after time
  5. Marked as used after reset
end note

' ============================================================================
' SECURITY & VALIDATION NOTES
' ============================================================================

note as ImplementationDetails
  **JPA Implementation Details**
  
  **Join Tables (Many-to-Many):**
  • user_roles: Links users to roles
  • post_tags: Categorizes posts with tags
  
  **Element Collection:**
  • user_visited_pages: Tracks user navigation
  
  **Cascade Strategies:**
  • CASCADE.ALL: Changes propagate to children
  • orphanRemoval: Deletes orphaned entities
  
  **Fetch Types:**
  • EAGER: Load immediately (roles, tags)
  • LAZY: Load on demand (posts, comments)
end note

note as SecurityFlow
  **Authentication & Security**
  
  **Registration Flow:**
  1. User submits credentials
  2. Password hashed with BCrypt
  3. Verification email sent
  4. User confirms email
  5. Account activated
  
  **Login Flow:**
  1. Credentials validated
  2. JWT token generated
  3. Token contains: id, username, roles
  4. Token sent to client
  5. Client includes token in requests
end note

